{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) The forward difference formula for the first derivative is:<br>", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_rBiYySe.png\" width=\"229\" height=\"50\"><br>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_sZ5wBgV.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"54\"><br>", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_nnA4k9p.png\" width=\"216\" height=\"57\"><br>", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_jq6k3sT.png\" width=\"306\" height=\"51\"><br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_VCCgkJC.png\" width=\"451\" height=\"161\"></p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) The central difference formula for the first derivative has an error of order:<br>", "option1": "O(h)<br>", "option2": "O(h<sup>2</sup>)<br>", "option3": "O(h<sup>3</sup>)<br>", "option4": "O(h<sup>4</sup>)<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Central difference is more accurate than forward/backward and has error of order h<sup>2</sup>, while forward/backward have error O(h).</p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which numerical integration rule requires that the number of subintervals nnn must be even?<br>", "option1": "Trapezoidal Rule<br>", "option2": "Simpson’s 1/3 Rule<br>", "option3": "Simpson’s 3/8 Rule<br>", "option4": "Midpoint Rule<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Simpson’s 1/3 rule works only if n is even, because it groups subintervals in pairs.</p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) If we apply Simpson’s 1/3 rule with n=2, it is equivalent to approximating the function with<br>", "option1": "A straight line<br>", "option2": "A quadratic polynomial<br>", "option3": "A cubic polynomial<br>", "option4": "A constant function<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>.Simpson’s 1/3 rule is derived by fitting a parabola (quadratic polynomial) through 3 points: f(x<sub>0</sub>),f(x<sub>1</sub>),f(x<sub>2</sub>).<br>That’s why it is more accurate than trapezoidal rule, which only fits a straight line.</p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following gives the best accuracy for the same step size h?<br>", "option1": "Trapezoidal Rule<br>", "option2": "Simpson’s 1/3 Rule<br>", "option3": "Simpson’s 3/8 Rule<br>", "option4": "Midpoint Rule<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Trapezoidal rule error: O(h<sup>2</sup>).<br>Midpoint rule error: O(h<sup>2</sup>).<br>Simpson’s 1/3 rule error: O(h<sup>4</sup>) → much smaller error.<br>Simpson’s 3/8 rule also has O(h<sup>4</sup>), but in practice 1/3 rule is often simpler and slightly better.</p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Given f(x) = x<sup>2</sup>. Use forward difference with step size h = 0.1 to approximate f‘(2).<br>", "option1": "4.1<br>", "option2": "4<br>", "option3": "4.41<br>", "option4": "3.9<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_m1HeKsq.png\" width=\"541\" height=\"234\"></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Let f(x) = 2x<sup>2 </sup>+ 1. Use central difference with step size h = 0.1 to approximate f‘(2)<br>", "option1": "7.8<br>", "option2": "7.9<br>", "option3": "8<br>", "option4": "8.1<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_WGLEPk8.png\" width=\"446\" height=\"224\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_6H5han3.png\" width=\"596\" height=\"53\"><br>", "option1": "Trapezoidal Rule<br>", "option2": "Simpson’s 1/3 Rule<br>", "option3": "Both<br>", "option4": "None<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Trapezoidal gave 0.375 (approx).<br>Simpson’s 1/3 gave 0.333 (exact).<br>Simpson’s rule is exact for polynomials up to degree 3.</p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) ‘For the same function f(x) = 2x<sup>2 </sup>+ 1, use backward difference with h=0.1 to approximate f′(2).<br>", "option1": "7.8<br>", "option2": "8<br>", "option3": "8.2<br>", "option4": "None<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_hRI2k2N.png\" width=\"498\" height=\"235\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_jLrTYRk.png\" width=\"787\" height=\"61\"><br>", "option1": "7.33<br>", "option2": "7.5<br>", "option3": "8<br>", "option4": "8.5<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_0OmPVju.png\" width=\"439\" height=\"207\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_0F3HlTd.png\" width=\"759\" height=\"47\"><br>", "option1": "8.67<br>", "option2": "8.5<br>", "option3": "9<br>", "option4": "8.33<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_lkj91xA.png\" width=\"437\" height=\"205\"></p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) For f(x) = x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3, approximate f‘(2) using central difference with h = 0.1.<br>", "option1": "3.9<br>", "option2": "4<br>", "option3": "4.1<br>", "option4": "7<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_m4rFvaW.png\" width=\"460\" height=\"216\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_zP3pbcG.png\" width=\"784\" height=\"54\"><br>", "option1": "14<br>", "option2": "13.8<br>", "option3": "14.2<br>", "option4": "14.25<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_WZ7jGx5.png\" width=\"356\" height=\"352\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_OlKVbO4.png\" width=\"760\" height=\"52\"><br>", "option1": "14<br>", "option2": "14.2<br>", "option3": "14.33<br>", "option4": "13.67<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": ""}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_AYGCcc1.png\" width=\"794\" height=\"50\"><br>", "option1": "7<br>", "option2": "6.67<br>", "option3": "6.5<br>", "option4": "None<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_Z1WEH1N.png\" width=\"426\" height=\"202\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_JitCqtM.png\" width=\"771\" height=\"36\"><br>", "option1": "5.9<br>", "option2": "6<br>", "option3": "6.1<br>", "option4": "6.2<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_aMBxiOu.png\" width=\"373\" height=\"124\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ckpWkT6.png\" width=\"770\" height=\"38\"><br>", "option1": "11.8<br>", "option2": "12<br>", "option3": "12.2<br>", "option4": "None<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_kgpQrXG.png\" width=\"571\" height=\"134\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_BmiFiTu.png\" width=\"753\" height=\"68\"><br>", "option1": "3.8<br>", "option2": "4<br>", "option3": "4.2<br>", "option4": "4.5<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_boDC1IR.png\" width=\"404\" height=\"138\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) The trapezoidal rule for integration is derived by approximating the curve by:<br>", "option1": "Straight lines<br>", "option2": "Parabolas<br>", "option3": "Cubic polynomials<br>", "option4": "None<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Trapezoidal rule assumes the area under the curve is made up of trapeziums formed by straight line joining successive points.</p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Which of the following numerical integration methods is exact for all polynomials up to degree 3?<br>", "option1": "Trapezoidal Rule<br>", "option2": "Midpoint Rule<br>", "option3": "Simpson’s 1/3 Rule<br>", "option4": "Simpson’s 3/8 Rule<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>Trapezoidal Rule → exact for degree ≤1<br>Midpoint Rule → exact for degree ≤1<br>Simpson’s 1/3 Rule → exact for degree ≤3<br>Simpson’s 3/8 Rule → exact for degree ≤3</p>\r\n<p>Exactness:</p>\r\n<p>Simpson’s 3/8 Rule is exact for cubic polynomials (degree ≤3), if the number of intervals is a multiple of 3.<br>That’s why in the MCQ about “exact for all polynomials up to degree 3,” 3/8 Rule was the correct choice.<br><br><strong>General Accuracy (for any smooth function, same step size h):</strong><br>Simpson’s 1/3 Rule is fourth-order accurate (error ∝ h<sup>4</sup>) and generally more efficient for most applications.<br>Simpson’s 3/8 Rule is also fourth-order accurate, but requires more points per segment (4 points), so it’s slightly less convenient.<br>Conclusion:</p>\r\n<p>If the question asks “best accuracy for the same step size”, Simpson’s 1/3 Rule  is usually preferred.<br>If the question asks “exact for cubic polynomials”, Simpson’s 3/8 Rule is safer.</p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_Xfb70Fq.png\" width=\"771\" height=\"44\"><br>", "option1": "1.01<br>", "option2": "1.1<br>", "option3": "1.05<br>", "option4": "1.2<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_5GdEWbz.png\" width=\"393\" height=\"35\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which of the following formulas corresponds to Heun’s method?<br>", "option1": "y<sub>n + 1</sub>​ = y<sub>n ​</sub>+ hf(x<sub>n</sub>​, y<sub>n</sub>​)<br>", "option2": "y<sub>n + 1</sub>​ = y<sub>n</sub>​ + (h​/2)[f(x<sub>n</sub>​, y<sub>n​</sub>) + f(x<sub>n + 1</sub>​, y<sub>n​ </sub>+ hf(x<sub>n​</sub>, y<sub>n​</sub>))]<br>", "option3": "y<sub>n + 1 ​</sub>= y<sub>n​ </sub>+ h​(k<sub>1​ </sub>+ 2k<sub>​2 </sub>+ 2k<sub>3 </sub>​+ k<sub>4​</sub>)/6<br>", "option4": "y<sub>n + 1</sub>​ = y<sub>n</sub>​ + hf(x<sub>n</sub>+1​,y<sub>n​</sub>)<br> <br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Heun’s method improves Euler by averaging the slope at the current point and the predicted next point.<br>This gives second-order accuracy (O(h<sup>2</sup>)), better than Euler.</p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) What is the order of accuracy of Euler’s method?<br>", "option1": "1<br>", "option2": "2<br>", "option3": "3<br>", "option4": "4<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Euler is a first-order method, meaning global error is proportional to h (O(h)). Reducing h improves accuracy linearly.</p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Which step is not part of Runge-Kutta 4 (RK4) Method?<br>", "option1": "k<sub>1</sub>​ = hf(x<sub>n</sub>​, y<sub>n</sub>​)<br>", "option2": "k<sub>2</sub>​ = hf(x<sub>n</sub>​ + h/2, y<sub>n</sub>​ + k<sub>1​</sub>/2)<br>", "option3": "k<sub>3​ </sub>= hf(x<sub>n</sub>​+ h/2, y<sub>n</sub>​ + k<sub>2</sub>​/2)<br>", "option4": "All are the part of RK4 Method<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>Steps A–C are part of RK4 slope calculations.<br>RK4 has fourth-order accuracy (O(h<sup>4</sup>)) → highly accurate for moderate h.</p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which method uses multiple previous points to compute the next value?<br>", "option1": "Euler<br>", "option2": "<span>RK4</span><br>", "option3": "Adams-Bashforth<br>", "option4": "All of these<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Multistep methods like Adams-Bashforth use previous computed points to predict y<sub>n+1</sub>, increasing efficiency for long computations.<br>Single-step methods (Euler, Heun, RK4) only use the current point.</p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Reducing the step size h in Euler’s method will:<br>", "option1": "Increase error<br>", "option2": "Decrease error<br>", "option3": "Have no effect<br>", "option4": "Make solution unstable<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Smaller h gives better slope approximation → lower truncation error.<br>However, too small h may increase round-off error in computer calculations.</p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which of the following is an initial value problem?<br>", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_1i0nduR.png\" width=\"175\" height=\"60\"><br>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/blobid0_MgFROaf.png\" width=\"283\" height=\"45\"><br>", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/blobid1_RZD0V2l.png\" width=\"189\" height=\"57\"><br>", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/blobid2_mtH6omt.png\" width=\"233\" height=\"42\"><br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>An IVP specifies both the derivative and initial condition.<br>Only option B provides y(x<sub>0</sub>​)=y<sub>0</sub>​, allowing step-by-step numerical solution.</p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_J0NgUxM.png\" width=\"768\" height=\"68\"><br>", "option1": "1`<br>", "option2": "1.1<br>", "option3": "1.2<br>", "option4": "1.3<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_smrttqA.png\" width=\"463\" height=\"32\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which is an initial value problem (IVP)?<br>", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_vUtnr98.png\" width=\"286\" height=\"92\"><br>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_QaWH2jA.png\" width=\"300\" height=\"45\"><br>", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_x27J6pz.png\" width=\"184\" height=\"62\"><br>", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_dpdhLiN.png\" width=\"326\" height=\"49\"><br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>IVP requires first derivative and initial value. Option B specifies y(0)=0. Option D is second-order, but only one initial condition is given → incomplete for an IVP.</p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_xm1u8lV.png\" width=\"699\" height=\"52\"><br>", "option1": "0.1<br>", "option2": "0.105<br>", "option3": "0.11<br>", "option4": "0.115<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_smoNqDU.png\" width=\"549\" height=\"94\"></p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Given:<br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_fhLCtOl.png\" width=\"407\" height=\"79\"><br><span>Compute </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></semantics></math></span></span><span> using </span><strong data-start=\"287\" data-end=\"305\">Euler’s method</strong><span>.</span><br>", "option1": "1.01<br>", "option2": "1.02<br>", "option3": "1.03<br>", "option4": "1.04<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_e5JTqw9.png\" width=\"416\" height=\"135\"></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Trapezoidal rule approximates an integral using:<br>", "option1": "Midpoint values only<br>", "option2": "Average of endpoints and interior points<br>", "option3": "Only left endpoint<br>", "option4": "Only right endpoint<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>It uses linear interpolation between points (endpoints + 2*sum of interior points).</p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩)  Which numerical method is fourth-order accurate?<br>", "option1": "Euler<br>", "option2": "Heun<br>", "option3": "Runge-Kutta 4<br>", "option4": "Trapezoidal<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><span>RK4 global error ∝ </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span><span class=\"pstrut\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>, very accurate even for moderate </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">.</span></span></span></span></p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) <span>Approximate </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f‘</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span> for </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></semantics></math></span></span><span> using </span><strong data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"887\">central difference</strong><span> with </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mspace\"></span><span class=\"mspace\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span></span></span></span><span>.</span><br>", "option1": "4<br>", "option2": "5<br>", "option3"